  "notes": [
    "Top-level GMD and social boards were moved and renamed only; existing children and bitmap fills were preserved.",
    "Eight imported tavus.io source frames were renamed by capture order and moved into a separate far-right source area; their imported contents were not edited.",
    "Existing reusable components and the canonical gmd-shared-* variables remain unchanged.",
    "Frame status and asset provenance remain board-level claims; index does not upgrade any study or draft to tested/ready.",
    "Native component examples are concentrated in 03.01â€“03.03; additional desktop/mobile application boards are not in this index snapshot.",
    "Egyptian motif atlas contains all 30 SVG assets translated into editable native paths and vector primitives using the source viewBox dimensions.",
    "Company desktop and 375px mobile boards are native editable compositions of the supplied company-page content; browser import was blocked by an active capture lock, so these are not captured HTML imports.",
    "Four material/photo fills render from relative image URLs (images/material-nile-faience.png, images/material-reed-papyrus.png, images/editorial-studio-pixel-register.png, images/editorial-family-pixel-interlace.png) copied beside the active Pen document; workspace source assets remain intact.",
    "Eight G2 source-informed constructions are represented as editable Pen vector paths on 06.03; each specimen retains the manifest ID, source IDs, group-part names, and intended use. These are contemporary adaptations, not direct tracings or historical reconstructions; only the 16×16 halftone cell has an explicit repeat claim.",
    "The 07.03 company extension is a native editable board adding collection evidence framing, the G2-014 visual-language chapter, FAQ, non-submitting contact-form specimen, and footer directory. The collection panel displays the full original EG-011 sheet via a relative image fill in contain mode; its visible label identifies it as the original, while rights review remains required before reuse.",
    "The corrected 06.03 atlas imports and 07.03 company chapter now use final G2-014 native path geometry with separated ink facets and paper-filled contour; the 06.03 specimen heading and component-part list identify the bird-like form. G2-022 class scoping and palette selectors are aligned with the final SVG bundle."
